# ── 301 REDIRECTS — FIX BROKEN INTERNAL LINKS ────────────────────────────────
# Plain mod_alias "Redirect 301" directives were not firing on the live host
# (LiteSpeed/Hostinger) despite mod_rewrite rules working — using RewriteRule
# for every legacy slug instead, since that mechanism is confirmed working live.
# Countries -> Best Betting Sites rename (2026-08-09, corrected same day):
# countries/<slug>/ was "Best Betting Sites in {Country}"; content now lives at
# best-betting-in-<slug>/ (see gen_best_betting_pages.py) — restored as its own
# distinct page after an earlier same-day rename briefly collapsed it into the
# bonus-focused best-bonus-in-<slug>/ page instead. Anchored with $ so this only
# matches the exact top-level country URL, never countries/<slug>/<city>/
# sub-pages, which stay at their existing path.
